Default template. To fetch SwiftData models in a view, you use the `@Query` property wrapper.

**Key concepts:**

1. `@Query` - automatically fetches and watches your models. When data changes, view updates.
2. `@Environment(\.modelContext)` - gives you access to add/delete models

**Basic pattern:**
```swift
import SwiftData

struct ContentView: View {
    @Query var tasks: [Task]

    var body: some View {
        List(tasks) { task in
            Text(task.title)
        }
    }
}
```

**But wait** - `List(tasks)` needs `Task` to be `Identifiable`. 

**Question:** Your Task model doesn't have `id` anymore (SwiftData handles it internally). How would you make `Task` conform to `Identifiable`? 

Hint: SwiftData models have a hidden `persistentModelID` property, but there's an easier way...

